<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gertrude of Merania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1185–1213</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gertrude of Merania (c. 1185–1213) was queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> as the first wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-ii-of-hungary">Andrew II</a>, and a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berthold-iv-duke-of-merania">Berthold IV, Duke of Merania</a>. Her favour towards her German relatives and courtiers caused resentment among the Hungarian nobility, and she was murdered by conspirators in 1213 while Andrew was on campaign. Her children included King Béla IV and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-of-hungary">Saint Elizabeth of Hungary</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gertrude-of-merania.jpg" alt="Gertrude of Merania" width="260" height="359" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User Caro1409 on de.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andreas_Getrude_Ungarn.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
